{:trait/id :trait-isr-jewish-diaspora-return-palestinian-conflict-coexistence-attempt, :trait/kind :value-system, :trait/region [:region/id "ISR"], :trait/title "Jewish diaspora return narrative, Palestinian conflict, attempted coexistence tensions", :trait/description "Israel (Jewish majority 74%, Arab minority 21%, Druze/others 5%) embodies diaspora return mythology & ongoing Palestinian conflict. Security concerns shape hypervigilance baseline. Kibbutz collectivism legacy; now mostly individualist startup culture. Arab Israelis face discrimination despite citizenship. Occupied territories create moral fractures.", :trait/contrast "NOT simple conflict; lived complexity of coexistence attempts.", :trait/confidence :medium, :trait/source "Hofstede; Barth (2013) 'Israeli Identity & the Israeli-Palestinian Conflict'; ethnographic studies", :trait/caveat "Tel Aviv cosmopolitan vs Haredi religious communities vastly different. Ashkenazi/Sephardi/Mizrahi Jewish ethnic stratifications. Arab Israelis marginalized in economy & politics. Palestinians (West Bank/Gaza) experience apartheid conditions. LGBTQ+ legal rights in Israel, but Palestinian LGBTQ+ face family/honor violence. Settlers on West Bank separate ideologically from mainstream Israeli society."}
