{:trait/id :trait-jpn-interdependence-amae, :trait/kind :value-system, :trait/region [:region/id "JPN"], :trait/title "Interdependence & amae (emotional dependence)", :trait/description "Japanese culture expects interdependence within relationships ('amae' = relying on other's benevolence). Self-sufficiency is not ideal; relational obligations drive life. Belonging to group (family, company) is primary identity.", :trait/contrast "CONTRAST to Western independence ideal: Japanese idealize relational belonging.", :trait/confidence :high, :trait/source "Doi (1973) 'Amae in Japanese Psychology'", :trait/caveat "Modernization & individualism challenge amae. Younger, educated cohorts embrace independence. International exposure reshapes expectations."}
